WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.420
Ever since Schitt's Creek hit the airwaves,
this heartfelt and hilarious show has charmed

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.300
and delighted countless viewers.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.000
But how much do you really know about the
show?

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.360
This is the untold truth of Schitt's Creek.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:19.420
Schitt's Creek tells the story of an eccentric
family unexpectedly thrust into extremely

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:20.300
close quarters.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:25.470
In the first minutes of the very first episode,
wealthy video store tycoon Johnny Rose suddenly

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:27.540
goes spectacularly broke.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:31.820
That means his family is forced to start all
over again in the small town of Schitt's Creek...

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:35.240
a town they purchased back in the day as a
snobby joke.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.760
"This town might just be your saving grace.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:39.940
At least for awhile."

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:40.940
"What do you mean?"

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.500
"You can live there for next to nothing, til
you get back on your feet."

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:47.860
Seeing as this is the story of a tight-knit
clan, it makes sense that the show's creator

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:51.700
Dan Levy would want to enlist members of his
own family for the project.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.900
And it certainly didn't hurt that his father
is Eugene Levy, a bonafide comedy legend.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:02.680
Eugene has had memorable roles in comedies
like American Pie and Best in Show, not to

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:06.760
mention '80s classics like National Lampoon's
Vacation and Splash.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:12.170
He got his start in the legendary improv group
The Second City in 1974, eventually going

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:17.900
on to star in the classic sketch comedy show
SCTV from 1976 to 1984.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:23.340
Eugene's son Dan also became a performer,
appearing regularly on MTV Canada.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:27.880
He eventually pitched the concept of Schitt's
Creek to his dad, and they subsequently created

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:28.900
the show together.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:31.080
The rest, as they say, is history.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:33.119
"David, help me with the doors."

00:01:33.119 --> 00:01:34.889
"No, I can't, I just got out of the shower?!"

00:01:34.889 --> 00:01:36.270
"I need help with the doors."

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:36.880
"Help!

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:37.380
Him!

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:37.880
With!

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:38.400
The!

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:38.900
Doors!"

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:39.400
"You help him with the doors!"

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:39.900
"Nooooo!"

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:43.420
And by the way, they aren't the only Levys
involved with the show.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:48.620
Sarah Levy, Dan's sister and Eugene's daughter,
plays the role of Twyla Sands, the waitress

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:50.160
at the town's only cafe.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:56.159
If the family dynamics feel a little too real
at times, it's probably because so many real-life

00:01:56.159 --> 00:01:57.929
family members worked on the show.

00:01:59.029 --> 00:02:04.270
Catherine O'Hara and Eugene Levy play Moira
and Johnny Rose, loving husband and wife and

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:06.260
proud parents to David and Alexis.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:10.819
Well, O'Hara and Eugene Levy actually have
quite the storied history together.

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:12.280
As The New York Times reports,

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:16.599
"[They] began performing together with other
like-minded comedians at the Second City club

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.460
in Toronto during the 1970s.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:23.040
[...] Mr. Levy and Ms. O’Hara honed their
skills and even briefly dated [...] before

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:25.460
gaining wider attention on SCTV.”

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:29.580
Later on, they appeared together in numerous
Christopher Guest comedies, including Waiting

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:32.420
for Guffman and Best in Show, to name just
a few.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.560
"She was very popular back then.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:36.140
She had dozens of boyfriends."

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:37.680
"Hundreds."

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:39.860
"Hundreds?"

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:45.840
In fact, Eugene Levy is the person who managed
to convince O'Hara to join Schitt's Creek

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.600
not that it really took all that much.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:51.160
Dan Levy was understandably thrilled with
this development.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:53.260
As he told The New York Times in 2015:

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:57.180
"I was not going to say, 'No, that's not a
good idea.'

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:00.640
When he offers up Catherine O'Hara, you take
it and run with it."

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:05.920
For her part, O'Hara barely hesitated before
signing on to the project, drawn in by Dan's

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:08.140
vision and the chance to work with Eugene
again.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:13.500
After studiously avoiding television projects,
O'Hara was hooked on the project right away.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.840
As she explained to Newsweek in 2019:

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:20.940
"Ever since SCTV, I've had an aversion to
locking into one character for any length

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:21.560
of time.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:26.120
But [Eugene Levy] convinced me to come to
a pilot presentation, and I loved it.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:27.100
He tricked me!"

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:33.680
Dan Levy plays the big-hearted but decidedly
standoffish David Rose, and as we mentioned,

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:35.940
he's the one who first came up with the idea
for the series.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:40.140
We wonder if you can guess the celebrity family
that inspired the idea…?

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:42.760
As he revealed to Out magazine in 2015:

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:47.920
"I had been watching some reality TV at the
time and was concentrating on what would happen

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:50.880
if one of these wealthy families would lose
everything.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:54.680
Would the Kardashians still be the Kardashians
without their money?"

00:03:55.180 --> 00:04:00.040
Using that idea as a springboard, Dan soon
got his father Eugene on board, knowing full

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:02.960
well that he had the comedy chops to pull
off the project.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:08.240
Obviously, Schitt's Creek's title features
a word that sounds exactly like a popular

00:04:08.249 --> 00:04:12.879
swear word — and perhaps unsurprisingly,
this fact managed to ruffled some feathers

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:14.900
before the show premiered on the CBC.

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:16.120
Bummer, huh?

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:17.440
"No.

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:19.180
Noooooooooo-wuh."

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:23.560
Initially, execs wanted the title changed
to something less scandalous.

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:27.720
In the hopes of swaying their opinions, the
Levys asked whether they'd be willing to run

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.380
a news story about someone named Schitt.

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:34.900
When the top brass said yes, the father and
son team literally went through a phone book

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:38.620
to prove that Schitt was, in fact, a real
last name.

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:43.310
The execs ultimately caved, and the Levys
got to name the show Schitt's Creek.

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:44.980
Quite the happy ending to this tale.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:50.220
Between playing David Rose and working behind
the scenes on Schitt's Creek, Dan Levy has

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:54.460
been a busy man over the last few years and
it looks like he'll only be getting busier

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.340
from here on out.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:05:01.180
In September 2019, he signed an incredible
deal with ABC to produce and create multiple

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:04.280
projects for the network and he's clearly
over the moon.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:05.620
He said in a statement:

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:10.600
"I’m thrilled to be partnering with ABC
Studios in this exciting next chapter.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:14.460
As I say a bittersweet goodbye to ‘Schitt’s
Creek,’ I look forward to the opportunity

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:19.050
and privilege to continue to tell inclusive
and meaningful stories that shine a positive

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:19.840
light out there.”

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:21.960
And what can we expect from this deal?

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:26.380
When The Hollywood Reporter asked Levy what
kinds of programming he wants to create for

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:27.919
the network, he replied:

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:34.300
"I feel like I can't not continue to make
television that means something and that advocates

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:37.260
for justice and equality and acceptance."

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:43.240
Alexis Rose is the spoiled yet sensitive daughter
of the Rose family and Canadian actress Annie

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:46.420
Murphy has played the part for the entire
run of Schitt's Creek.

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:50.620
But even though it proved to be her breakout
role, she actually wasn't the first person

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:51.900
cast as Alexis.

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:57.440
Believe it or not, Saturday Night Live alum
Abby Elliott was originally slated to play

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:57.940
Alexis.

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:02.440
Incidentally, her father is Chris Elliott,
who appears on Schitt's Creek as the terminally

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:04.860
crass town mayor Roland Schitt.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:08.990
The role became available after Abby abruptly
left the project.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:14.280
But as fate would have it, Murphy was already
on hand after auditioning to play Stevie Budd,

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:18.830
the Rosebud Motel's brilliantly sarcastic
proprietor a role that later went to actress

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:19.820
Emily Hampshire.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.940
However, there was a problem.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.940
As Murphy revealed to Vulture in April 2018,

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.320
"I was a brunette when I auditioned.

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:31.340
And Eugene was having a really, really hard
time wrapping his head around the fact that

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:34.160
Alexis is blonde and Annie Murphy is brunette.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:38.960
He couldn’t quite get there, so Dan had
to tape pictures of blonde hair on my picture.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:41.660
It finally got through to him, thank goodness."

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:43.180
Thank goodness is right.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:48.680
Murphy is utterly brilliant in the role, and
we could listen to her say "David" all day.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:49.800
"David.

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:50.840
Nobody cares."

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:51.860
"You know what, David?

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:54.570
You get murdered first for once."

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:57.720
"Well, I'm not going to wear my own clothes
into the room, David."

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:01.840
Since the likes of Eugene Levy and Catherine
O'Hara are involved, it should come as no

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:05.540
surprise that Schitt's Creek features more
than a few musical performances.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:10.300
In fact, some of the show's most memorable
musical moments were crafted by the stars

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:15.360
of the show, including a moving serenade during
an open mic from the series' fourth season.

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:20.140
Patrick is David's boyfriend and business
partner, played to perfection by actor Noah

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:22.720
Reid, an accomplished musician in his own
right.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:27.120
In the episode in question, he organizes an
open mic night to help promote their store

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:28.500
Rose Apothecary.

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:34.000
David is initially horrified, but he ends
up being absolutely bowled over by Patrick's

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.300
performance of Tina Turner's "The Best."

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:41.820
Reid created the arrangement himself and thus
helped create one of the show's most romantic

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:42.320
moments.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:47.879
As for other musical highlights, we'd be remiss
not to mention Alexis's Cabaret audition in

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:48.879
season five.

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:54.039
"I have chosen to perform the title track
off of my critically reviewed limited reality

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:55.400
series A LIttle Bit Alexis."

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:56.060
"Oh!"

00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:58.680
The song includes such immortal lines as:

00:07:58.780 --> 00:08:03.940
"I'm a Lamborghini / I'm a Hollywood star
/ I'm a little bit tipsy / When I drive my

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:10.520
car / I'm expensive sushi / I'm a cute huge
yacht / I'm a little bit single / Even when

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:11.140
I'm not."

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:15.800
"I'm a little bit … la la la la la la … a
little bit Alexis…"

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:19.260
Annie Murphy wrote the song herself with the
help of a few friends.

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:23.700
And we should probably mention the throbbing
club mix of the song, which is available on

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:28.169
Spotify as we speak — and which is basically
beyond belief.

00:08:28.169 --> 00:08:30.000
"I'm hoping to tour Japan."

00:08:30.949 --> 00:08:33.760
"We're going to do a full international release
with it."

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:36.720
"I'm hoping it's going to go to Number One
on, like, multiple charts."

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:42.260
Schitt's Creek has plenty of running gags
and one of the best is Moira's completely

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:43.830
unidentifiable accent.

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:50.140
"In the lea of a picturesque ridge lies a
small unpretentious winery."

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:55.200
That accent is quite literally all over the
place… and O'Hara has a real knack for stretching

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.760
a single word to the point of ridiculousness.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:02.660
"I'm going to resurrect 'One Crazy Summer:
The Patty Hearst story.'

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:07.780
It's a tale of perseverance much like your
quest to bring asbestos back to the town."

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:11.930
O'Hara revealed her inspiration in a 2019
interview with Newsweek:

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:16.760
"I've met people whose accents have nothing
to do with where they were born or raised

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:18.860
they want to reinvent themselves.

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:23.160
[...] Everything about Moira comes from the
potential she believes she has."

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:27.240
O'Hara goes on to cite Madonna and Audrey
Hepburn as influences.

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:30.080
As for her signature syllable stretching,
she says:

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:36.080
"I want to have Moira learn a new word every
day to not only educate herself but to educate

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:37.340
everyone in the town.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:42.960
Then, using the new vocabulary, which I wish
I could retain, I love to stretch out the

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:43.620
syllables.

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:47.670
I don't think about it when I'm doing it,
but some words want to live longer."

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:49.900
"Are the pillows feather or foam?"

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:50.640
"Yes."

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:52.300
"Sorry, which one?"

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:53.120
"I don't care."

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:53.740
"I'm sorry?"

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:55.080
"I don't know?"

00:09:55.960 --> 00:10:00.780
After filming was completed on Schitt's Creek
sixth and final season, the cast took home

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:02.300
some of their favorite props.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:07.700
As Variety reports, Dan Levy took home the
framed first receipt from Rose Apothecary,

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:11.180
which Patrick gives to David on what we can
safely call their first date.

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:17.600
"If there is anything remotely sentimental
in here, he is on a date with you right now."

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:22.040
Eugene Levy took home a few portraits of the
Rose family no big deal.

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:27.320
Catherine O'Hara snatched up several of Moira's
wigs and some of her jewelry, and Annie Murphy

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:30.270
took home Alexis' mistyped college degree.

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:34.980
Meanwhile, more than 800 high-end wardrobe
pieces from Schitt's Creek went on sale in

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:40.410
October 2019 through Canadian retailer VSP
Consignment, and some of the proceeds were

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:43.020
donated to the education organization GLSEN.

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:44.800
According to the official website,

00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:50.020
"[It's an organization that] works to ensure
that LGBTQ students are able to learn and

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:53.260
grow in a school environment free from bullying
and harassment."

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:57.880
Although it's a comedy through and through,
Schitt's Creek certainly doesn't shy away

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:04.020
from sentimentality and some of its best scenes
and storylines explore modern love and relationships.

00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:09.120
For example, following an unexpected night
of passion between Stevie and David in Season

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:13.000
One, David uses a clever wine-based analogy
to explain his preferences.

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:14.020
As he puts it,

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:15.500
"I like the wine and not the label.

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:16.780
Does that make sense?"

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:17.600
"Yes.

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:18.660
It does."

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:23.720
Meanwhile, when Patrick comes out to his parents
in Season Five, the result is one of the most

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:26.000
touching television scenes in recent memory.

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:31.320
Thanks to his precise, loving touch when it
comes to the show, Dan Levy frequently receives

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:32.850
letters from fans and viewers.

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:36.940
They thank him for making them stronger, or
for helping them accept loved ones who are

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:38.540
struggling with their identities.

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:44.500
It's no wonder Levy won a GLAAD Award in 2019
for championing LGBTQ acceptance through his

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:48.550
work in Schitt's Creek, and he delivered a
characteristically heartfelt and thoughtful

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:50.180
speech at the annual gala:

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:55.620
"Almost three quarters of LGBT youths, they
say they are more honest about themselves

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:57.990
online than in the real world."

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:03.670
The fictional world of Schitt's Creek might
feel far removed from reality at times, but

00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:08.430
as the show has surged in popularity, real-life
versions of the adorable small town have been

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:10.240
popping up more and more frequently.

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:11.520
Let us explain.

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:17.220
In October 2019, Schitt's Creek unveiled two
interactive pop-ups in New York City and Los

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:17.760
Angeles.

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:22.240
Lucky guests got to wander through some of
the show's most iconic settings including

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:28.120
the Rose family's motel rooms, the town diner
Cafe Tropical, and David and Patrick's business,

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:29.120
Rose Apothecary.

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:34.000
Meanwhile, as the show's final season started
airing, Netflix teamed up with Beekman 1802

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:39.700
to create a line called, unsurprisingly, "Rose
Apothecary x Beekman 1802."

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:44.500
These scented bath and body products look
exactly like the merchandise supposedly being

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:46.020
sold at the fictional shop.

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:47.600
The signature scent?

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:48.860
Rose, naturally.

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:54.200
Made with goat milk, these Schitt's Creek-inspired
goodies are a perfect tie-in to the show.

00:12:55.060 --> 00:13:00.300
We're sure David would wholeheartedly approve…
as much as he's capable of approving of anything.

00:13:00.640 --> 00:13:01.640
"Uh-oh."

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:03.200
"What is…?

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:04.160
Is something wrong?"

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:05.080
"No.

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:09.540
They're just new… mints that haven't been
sampled yet so for all we know, they could

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:10.040
be poison."

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:15.640
In Summer 2019, it was announced that Schitt's
Creek had earned four Emmy nominations, with

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:17.140
Deadline reporting that

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:22.780
"[The show] landed noms in the Comedy Series,
Lead Actor Comedy Series [for Eugene Levy],

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:27.680
Lead Actress Comedy Series [for Catherine
O’Hara], and Contemporary Costumes categories."

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:33.520
The cast was understandably thrilled and Schitt's
Creek became the first PopTV show to ever

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:35.140
earn an Emmy nomination.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:38.620
